# The Firewall parity table: origin/main's Firewall screen and hardn -w against the Firewall control
# on the engine (refactor plan slice 4, unit (b2), next/s4-parity; docs/engine/parity-firewall.md).
# Generated by TestParity (pkg/screens/firewall); make golden-update rewrites it. Do not edit.
# origin/main: pkg/characterization's goldens, read in place, which are origin/main plus the trunk's
# gates (parity-firewall.md §2): menu/firewall_* (TestLegacyMenuFirewall, TestLegacyMenuDryRun; Debian 13
# fixtures, or Proxmox VE on them), ops/configure_secure_firewall (TestOperationGoldens; hardn -w) and
# ops/configure_secure_firewall_profiles (menu item 2). ufw is the fixture's: it takes ufw reset as done, which probably aborts on a
# real host (V9, [I]). The new path: the Firewall screen's Run (unit (c), next/s4-screen), typed as a
# user types it, or Incoming{ActionEnable} through the engine (-w), on hostfake: written, not run (gate 5).
# Where no item leads to the action, the key is refused, and the cell says so.
# Sources: V<n> side-effects.md §8, named by the cell's golden; decision <n>, Made here, §6's words
# gallery-firewall.md §5, §6 (adopted 2026-11-01); defect <n> its §2; P-16, P-30, P-33 as decided;
# control-firewall.md's calls, each "engineering call, not adopted by the maintainer"; parity-firewall.md
# §6's four differences, adopted 2026-11-02.

== enable on Debian 13
host: ufw inactive, no rules, sshd on 2230 (forced: the fixture's start, with sshd as the row says, not read from Debian 13's stock install)
origin/main: menu/firewall_item1_inactive_enable_runs_configure.golden (V9)
  start: Debian 13; ufw inactive, no rules; cfg.SshPort 2230; 0 profiles; dryRun false
  probes: which ufw -> ok; ufw status -> ok; dpkg-query -W "--showformat=${Status}" pve-manager -> ok; which ufw -> ok; which ufw -> ok; ufw status -> ok
  run ufw default deny incoming
  run ufw default allow outgoing
  run ufw disable
  run ufw reset
  run ufw allow 2230/tcp comment "SSH access"
  run sh -c "yes | ufw enable"
new path: the Firewall screen, typed 1, host-01: the hostname typed; -w's plan and apply leave the same
  probes: sshd -T -f /etc/ssh/sshd_config; ss -Htln; ufw status verbose; systemctl is-enabled ufw.service; ss -Htlnp; ss -Hulnp
  write /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service 0644, atomic
    | # hardn's boot unit (P-34 (c); docs/safety/revert-boot.md). hardn installs
    | # it before it arms the revert timer of a change that could lock you out, and
    | # removes it at a boot that finds no change journalled.
    | #
    | # At boot, before sshd reads its files: re-arm the revert timer of a change
    | # waiting for "hardn confirm", for what remains of its window, or roll the
    | # change back when its deadline has passed. Ordering only: sshd starts
    | # whatever this unit does.
    | [Unit]
    | Description=hardn: re-arm or run the revert timer of an unconfirmed change
    | DefaultDependencies=no
    | After=local-fs.target sysinit.target ufw.service
    | Before=ssh.service ssh.socket sshd.service sshd.socket shutdown.target
    | Conflicts=shutdown.target
    |
    | [Service]
    | Type=oneshot
    | RemainAfterExit=yes
    | ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/hardn rollback --boot
    | TimeoutStartSec=7min
    |
    | [Install]
    | WantedBy=multi-user.target
  run ufw allow 2230/tcp
  run ufw --force enable
  backup: none; journal: journalled first; findings: none
agree  refusal: none
agree  profile file: none
agree  directories: none
agree  backup: none
agree  findings: none
agree  hardn.yml: not saved
agree  ufw after: active
agree  rules after: 2230/tcp
agree  SSH rule added: 2230/tcp
agree  at boot: not changed
agree  packages: none
differ files: none | /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service 0644
       defect 3's answer (§5): through the flow, the hostname typed, confirm-or-revert armed: hardn's boot unit, the engine's for any lockout-risk plan; it stays after a rollback, until a boot finds nothing journalled
differ commands: ufw default deny incoming, ufw default allow outgoing, ufw disable, ufw reset, ufw allow 2230/tcp comment "SSH access", sh -c "yes | ufw enable" | ufw allow 2230/tcp, ufw --force enable
       V9; defect 1; Made here: default deny, default allow outgoing, disable and reset gone; the allow, then the start (the comment and the start's form are rows of their own)
differ journal: none | journalled first
       defect 3's answer (§5): through the flow, the hostname typed, confirm-or-revert armed: no rollback; now journalled first
differ asks: nothing | the hostname typed; the timer armed
       defect 3's answer (§5): through the flow, the hostname typed, confirm-or-revert armed: one key, no question; now the hostname typed, the timer armed
differ rule comment: SSH access | none
       parity-firewall.md §6, adopted 2026-11-02: the SSH rule's comment, SSH access, is gone: ufw status no longer names it
