agree  rules after: 2230/tcp
agree  SSH rule added: 2230/tcp
agree  at boot: not changed
agree  packages: none
differ files: none | /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service 0644
       decision 4: hardn's boot unit, the engine's for any lockout-risk plan: the timer unit (d)'s question arms
differ commands: ufw default deny incoming, ufw default allow outgoing, ufw disable, ufw reset, ufw allow 2230/tcp comment "SSH access", sh -c "yes | ufw enable" | ufw allow 2230/tcp, ufw --force enable
       V9; defect 1; Made here: as enable, on -w
differ journal: none | journalled first
       decision 4: no rollback; now journalled first
differ asks: nothing | the timer armed; the hostname typed in unit (d) (decision 4)
       decision 4: no question; the plan arms the timer, and unit (d) adds the hostname typed, off a terminal a refusal
differ rule comment: SSH access | none
       parity-firewall.md §6, adopted 2026-11-02: the SSH rule's comment, SSH access, is gone: ufw status no longer names it
differ how ufw starts: sh -c "yes | ufw enable" | ufw --force enable
       parity-firewall.md §6, adopted 2026-11-02; docs/safety/ufw.md §3: sh -c "yes | ufw enable"; now ufw --force enable
